<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Odoardo Farnese, Duke of Parma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1612">1612</a>–<a href="/years/1646">1646</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Odoardo I Farnese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Odoardo Farnese was duke of Parma and Piacenza from 1622. Seeking military glory, he allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1635, bringing a devastating Spanish invasion of the Piacenza countryside until he made peace in 1637. He then fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-castro">First War of Castro</a> in 1641–1644 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-viii">Pope Urban VIII</a> and the Barberini family to keep his family's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fief">fief</a> of Castro.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/odoardo-farnese-duke-of-parma.jpg" alt="Odoardo Farnese, Duke of Parma" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Isacco Gioacchino Levi (1818-1908) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ritratto_di_Odoardo_Farnese.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Duke <b>Odoardo Farnese</b>, ambitious for glory, allied with France in 1635 during the Thirty Years’ War, and Spanish troops ravaged the Piacenza countryside until he made peace in 1637.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Duchy of Parma and Piacenza · Military</a></li></ul></section>
